Hi @kiranpal18 The easiest way to get good results from LLMs is to begin with a full code example. So, show an LLM some working code either from this competition's public sharing or an old competition's public sharing.

Next if you are learning, ask the LLM to explain the code to you. You can use this new understanding to play with the code yourself a little. i.e. after understanding the purpose of hyperparameters or features, you can try tuning/changing some (and watching the result on cv score).

Lastly, you can ask the LLM to improve the code. You can suggest a new idea that you know or that you have read about in the forums or research paper. Or you can just ask LLM to suggest a possible improvement. During the whole process, ask the LLM to explain what and why it is doing.

Run the new code and see if it achieves a better local CV score. Repeat the above process over and over.


